    "done_when": "Defect: the accepted-path peer-claim check in reckon/crew/promotion.py (the loop whose refusal reads \"cannot accept reckon/cli.py: live run ... claims reckon/cli.py\") refuses a path any live peer run claims, including a path on the project's shared-write list that dispatch deliberately admits co-claims on. So a run whose merged change touched a shared file cannot be promoted while any peer co-claims that file. First confirm it reproduces at base through the public completion entry point. Done when an accepted path that is on the project's shared-write list is accepted even while a live peer run claims it, using the same shared-path resolver dispatch already uses (reuse it, never re-read the list a second way); a co-claimed path NOT on the shared-write list is still refused with the existing message; and a peer claim on a directory that merely contains a shared file still refuses any non-shared path under it. Do not change acceptance semantics otherwise. Assert through the completion entry point over a temporary repository with a live peer pointer whose worker pid is alive, under a temporary config home with the real config home asserted untouched. At least one added assertion must fail at the dispatch base. Measured over tests/test_crew_promotion_scope.py plus tests/test_crew_promotion.py in ONE invocation: zero added failures against base. Report ruff findings on the staged paths against the count at base.",
